body:
Read the paragraph aloud. Does each sentence prepare for the next? A transition should express an actual relationship, not simply add “therefore” before the thesis.

Remove:

- sweeping openings such as “Since the beginning of time…”;
- dictionary definitions and generic claims about society;
- a long retelling of the passage;
- unsupported claims about the author’s intentions or every reader’s reaction;
- statements announcing that you are about to write an essay.

A short opening about the topic can work if it leads directly into the text. A hook is optional; do not spend time manufacturing one.
